iv Introduction The increasing use of computers to store information, together with the increasing necessity for the communication of dental information by wire, printed documents and orally, has required that new basic elements be taken into consideration for drawing up a designation system for teeth. The system described in this International Standard was originally drawn up by the FDI World Dental Federation and approved by the World Health Organization (WHO) and Technical committee ISO/TC 106, Dentistry, to satisfy the following requirements:
a) simple to understand and teach;
b) easy to pronounce in conversation and dictation;
c) readily communicable in print and by wire;
d) easy to translate into computer “input”;
e) easily adaptable to standard charts used in general dental practice.

Who can use FDI Policy Statements?
FDI PSs are intended to serve as a reference to the global oral health community. However, they can also be used by the general public, policymakers, educators, the media, and/or representatives of any social group wishing to reduce the burden of oral disease.
How to use FDI Policy Statements FDI PSs can be used by all oral health professionals for education, advocacy, legislation, public relations and implementation of national oral health policies within their respective countries.
What FDI PSs can help you with:
✓✓Forming and supporting your NDA’s official positions and statements;
✓✓Advocating your NDA’s positions to decision-makers;
✓✓Drafting health legislation;
✓✓Educating people about oral health;
✓✓Raising awareness on oral disease;
✓✓Creating agendas of scientific events;
✓✓Engaging with third party funders.
Target audience groups:
✓✓Oral health professionals (dental and maxillofacial surgeons, dentists, dental team members, hygienists, etc.) ✓✓General Public (patients, representatives of different social, gender and age groups) ✓✓Decision-makers (state and regional health and educational authorities, government members, policymakers, etc.) ✓✓Sponsors (third party funders, donors)
